      "writtenOn": "2022-08-18T23:05:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Caveh,\nI think we should leave the reserved bit field as part of the RMDO. I did not include the reserved field in the initial implementation of this, but then added it during the review. Basically, we know the partner will send us a 32-bit RMDO with bits 0-15 reserved. Defining the RMDO this way allows us to directly copy what we get from the partner to our internal state. If we remove the reserved field, we will also need to update how we assign the partner RMDO after receiving a Revision message.\n\npreviously talked about here: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3607054/comment/017c6913_0d99f6b5/",
      "parentUuid": "be0b6343_5553a77a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 589,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 589,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "572d1dc02a0c82b8c783a860a56f90d5df3e33f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06e2d144_0634058c",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T20:54:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i\u0027m not convinced mixing data types here helps specify the data format\nclearly to the reader.\nideally they should all be uint32_t with the appropriate width bit\nfield. i think you\u0027re lucky here that the bit fields fit nicely into\nbytes. if that weren\u0027t the case, i think this style of declaration\nwould inadvertently lead to bit padding.",
      "parentUuid": "814750cd_ff630bee",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 589,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 589,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "572d1dc02a0c82b8c783a860a56f90d5df3e33f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c823b6a_8ea56815",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-22T21:33:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I see how storing the data this way would not extend to other PD data objects based on field size. Would you prefer we store the RMDO as a uint32_t and use shifting/masking to get field values?",
      "parentUuid": "06e2d144_0634058c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 589,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 589,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "572d1dc02a0c82b8c783a860a56f90d5df3e33f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d14426d4_7407d748",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-23T02:38:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "no need for explicit shift/mask. if each member is a uint32_t,\nthe fields get packed by definition. i really don\u0027t know what happens\nwhen you mix types for fields that are intended to be contiguous.\n\nif you want to go overboard on field accessors, we could do something like\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3263231\nbut that\u0027s way beyond the scope of fixing a basic bug.",
      "parentUuid": "6c823b6a_8ea56815",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 589,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 589,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "572d1dc02a0c82b8c783a860a56f90d5df3e33f9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
